A few weeks ago we decided to start analyzing all this data." hash="d11f66d1d46ae89b043f296cc37d01c7" href="http://blog.stephenwolfram.com/2013/04/data-science-of-the-facebook-world/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[post_blog]  visualization  information  statistics  sociology  science  math  social_network  !  !!  graph  network" time="2013-04-25T00:43:32Z"/><post description="bl.ocks.org/mbostock/raw/5446416/e46a4985e7a851f10bc231d1e78681c457d94aad/" extended="interactive panorama of the Milky Way" hash="86cfab968daf86f9dc2ba3c44d50a36a" href="http://bl.ocks.org/mbostock/raw/5446416/e46a4985e7a851f10bc231d1e78681c457d94aad/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[project]  photography  space  astronomy  interaction  " time="2013-04-23T21:32:11Z"/><post description="Where Does My Tweet Go?" extended="The speed at which Twitter spreads information is fascinating. Yet looking at your timeline it’s not always easy to grasp how tweets participated to the show. To enable you to get a perfect understanding of how tweets spread, we created WDMTG." hash="82aa3dc2a97dae7724cdcf661966ce17" href="http://wdmtg.com/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="twitter visualization text time ! tree sociology social_network [project] !! 3D networks" time="2013-04-23T14:30:01Z"/><post description="Bach, Preludio, Partita in E Major, Lara St. John, solo violin" extended="simple visualization of violin notes on score" hash="c8855f9ab66e44adb9f36fd1141b4336" href="http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uoqFH-i7jYY&amp;sns=tw" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[video_youtube]  music  sound  visualization  time  frequencies  !  " time="2013-04-23T12:25:16Z"/><post description="Mapping the Human ‘Diseasome’" extended="Researchers created a map linking different diseases, represented by circles, to the genes they have in common, represented by squares." hash="437880faff65fc09506f3dcf3d00a194" href="http://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2008/05/05/science/20080506_DISEASE.html?_r=0" private="no" shared="yes" tag="genetics visualization graph [project] health networks biology" time="2013-04-22T00:00:37Z"/><post description="Telescopic Text © Joe Davis 2008" extended="a tree structured tree, that starts short and grows by opening nodes" hash="9dae1ec828d080b9be11cd9e836cecff" href="http://telescopictext.com/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[project]  interaction  narrative  text  tree  bifurcation  !  literature  poetry  " time="2013-04-19T16:22:13Z"/><post description="Why No One Clicked on the Great Hypertext Story" extended="interesting reflection about nonlinear storytelling and his history in internet" hash="a4c6987c8fd1863fc12914105719b6d5" href="http://www.wired.com/magazine/2013/04/hypertext/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[post_blog]  narrative  bifurcation  text  books  internet  history  sociology  " time="2013-04-18T23:20:41Z"/><post description="For the Elderly, Diseases That Overlap" extended="Elder people with multiple chronic diseases, visualization based in Euler diagrams" hash="15df28498fe2a379a930aa2398053445" href="http://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/04/16/science/disease-overlap-in-elderly.html" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[project]  visualization  health  sociology  statistics  " time="2013-04-18T19:02:29Z"/><post description="Inequality and New York's subway" extended="The interactive infographic here charts these shifts, using data on median income, from the U.S. Census Bureau, for census tracts with subway stations. " hash="b0178bb2d9a994244fd59a07d3e84d4c" href="http://www.newyorker.com/sandbox/business/subway.html" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[project]  visualization  New-York_USA  information  economy  sociology  travel  " time="2013-04-18T19:00:29Z"/><post description="Kepler’s Tally of Planets - Interactive Feature - NYTimes.com" extended="visualization of exoplanets &quot;NASA’s Kepler mission has discovered more than 100 confirmed planets orbiting distant stars. Planets with a known size and orbit are shown below, including five planets orbiting Kepler 62, announced this week.&quot;" hash="41b51ef1d5db70c36d1eacec8f239917" href="http://www.nytimes.com/interactive/science/space/keplers-tally-of-planets.html?smid=tw-share" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[project]  visualization  astronomy  education  circle  space  frequencies  !  " time="2013-04-18T18:55:50Z"/><post description="Anscombe's quartet" extended="Anscombe's quartet comprises four datasets that have nearly identical simple statistical properties, yet appear very different when graphed. Each dataset consists of eleven (x,y) points. They were constructed in 1973 by the statistician Francis Anscombe to demonstrate both the importance of graphing data before analyzing it and the effect of outliers on statistical properties." hash="0f9f1a56357ac24e4a033a5fa8dda5bb" href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anscombe_s_quartet" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[wikipedia_article]  statistics  visualization  math  numbers  " time="2013-04-12T15:16:00Z"/><post description="Cartogram Types" extended="About different types of cartograms  &quot;A cartogram is a type of graphic that depicts attributes of geographic objects as the object's area. Because a cartogram does not depict geographic space, but rather changes the size of objects depending on a certain attribute, a cartogram is not a true map.&quot;" hash="f582f3d53b330df3c33ec136c53f632a" href="http://www.ncgia.ucsb.edu/projects/Cartogram_Central/types.html" private="no" shared="yes" tag="visualization  map  gis  geography  geometry  algorithm  space  topology  information  " time="2013-04-12T12:49:32Z"/><post description="15 Common Movie Poster Themes" extended="strong stereotypes in movies posters design" hash="163c4459a48896c529ebe0e7be2b0850" href="http://www.buzzfeed.com/pauljamez/15-common-movie-poster-themes-2kjh" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[post_blog]  [compilation]  movies  image  design  narrative  photography  sociology  " time="2013-04-10T15:31:22Z"/><post description="650 Million Years in under 2 minutes" extended="Pangea reunited, beautiful animation of continents wandering" hash="4c7ca34542eb12f93529040ca21a28cf" href="http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NYbTNFN3NBo&amp;feature=player_embedded" private="no" shared="yes" tag="history geology visualization time geography animation education [video_youtube] science" time="2013-04-08T21:32:28Z"/><post description="Visualizing Our Favorite TV Shows | Visual.ly Blog" extended="compilation of TV shows visualizations" hash="8cde2c033c3b51e6b1bf0e1fb89dc59a" href="http://blog.visual.ly/visualizing-our-favorite-tv-shows/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="visualization [post_blog] narrative popular tv [compilation] video" time="2013-04-08T13:30:41Z"/><post description="Learning to See | Information Architects" extended="Our mind is not a camera. Seeing is not a passive act. We see what we expect to see, or, as Ana&amp;iuml;s Nin put it so beautifully: “We don’t see things as they are, we see them as we are.”" hash="4720a3cfb69f43e9c6cf411dee1b6a44" href="http://informationarchitects.net/blog/learning-to-see/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[post_blog] ! narrative psychology perception brain design" time="2013-04-08T13:19:00Z"/><post description="Context: Take leadership from the most impacted" extended="This is an experimental interface for Beautiful Trouble: A Toolbox For Revolution. Beautiful Trouble is a book and web toolbox that puts the accumulated wisdom of decades of creative protest into the hands of the next generation of change-makers." hash="80898253ada12f16d3d2d887395dc8b9" href="http://www.explore.beautifultrouble.org/#1:take-leadership-from-the-most-impacted" private="no" shared="yes" tag="books visualization graph violence sociology art [project] networks" time="2013-03-29T23:09:25Z"/><post description="Metropolitain.io - A visual and interactive experiment on the Parisian underground network" extended="isochronic map + crowds heatmap Paris metro visualization &quot;This visualization offers to challenge this conventional view. Metropolitain takes on an unexpected gamble: using cold, abstract figures to take the pulse of a hectic and feverish metropolis.&quot;" hash="a1c91e54563cf97321e3bf37513ef423" href="http://metropolitain.io/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[project]  visualization  Paris_France  travel  city  map  time  graph  !  " time="2013-03-26T13:22:42Z"/><post description="Fractal Cities" extended="classic book on cities analysis and simulation based on fractals " hash="02266d81110773cf9284eef41e454aec" href="http://www.fractalcities.org/book/Fractal%20Cities%20Low%20Resolution.pdf" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[pdf]  [book]  city  fractals  simulation  code  algorithm  digital_arts  !  " time="2013-03-23T04:43:50Z"/><post description="Hooktheory" extended="complex online application based on the analysis of chords in 1300 songs / contains a Markov chain of chords." hash="1e4bf8410f02ddc55b78d9abf68e0b2b" href="http://www.hooktheory.com/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="music visualization time ! graph sound popular [project] !! culture statistics" time="2013-03-21T16:15:34Z"/><post description="The Power of Swarms Can Help Us Fight Cancer, Understand the Brain, and Predict the Future" extended="&amp;quot;Now, thanks to new observation technologies, powerful software, and statistical methods, the mechanics of collectives are being revealed. Indeed, enough physicists, biologists, and engineers have gotten involved that the science itself seems to be hitting a density-dependent shift. Without obvious leaders or an overarching plan, this collective of the collective-obsessed is finding that the rules that produce majestic cohesion out of local jostling turn up in everything from neurons to human beings.&amp;quot;" hash="ba34b2b13504e26a760edacba7e48ca7" href="http://www.wired.com/wiredscience/2013/03/powers-of-swarms/all/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[post_blog] chaos animals ! !!! !! emergence simulation science algorithm math life biology" time="2013-03-20T17:19:10Z"/><post description="stacksort" extended="In a recent xkcd's alt text, Randall Munroe suggested stacksort, a sort that searches StackOverflow for sorting functions and runs them until it returns the correct answer. So, I made it. If you like running arbitrary code in your browser, try it out." hash="48f441a06d52c4ccc26ef8b7608bef37" href="http://gkoberger.github.com/stacksort/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[project]  humor  math  code  algorithm  " time="2013-03-18T19:03:14Z"/><post description="Resonet - mapping the twitter community around the resonate festival" extended="This map shows a selection of 2114 Twitter accounts related to the resonate festival and their 175’380 followership relations. We collected all Twitter users that are followed by a list of seed accounts (festival speakers, organizers and attendees). This map presents a selection of users that are followed by at least 8 people in this extended network." hash="8b7bf154d73cc8c6e33331d39806c38c" href="http://moritz.stefaner.eu/projects/resonet/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[project]  network  visualization  twitter  interface  interaction  !" time="2013-03-18T14:43:22Z"/><post description="All 135 Space Shuttle launches at once" extended="collage of videos displaying all the Space Shuttle launches synchronized (including Challenger)" hash="0dc55ed32dc47bdb3c80d8362c584ed0" href="http://kottke.org/12/07/all-135-space-shuttle-launches-at-once" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[project]  [video]  space  technology  collage  video  narrative  history  time  !  !!  astronomy  " time="2013-03-16T18:06:37Z"/><post description="Mutliple videos at once" extended="collection of videos of videos synchronized (100 Messi goals at once f.i.)" hash="18a374a112ce1de0d4bbfe0d742e22e3" href="http://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLBGo_u3nwqxPlmGHlQlHR2SCexsEsLLkR&amp;feature=view_all" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[compilation]  [meta_compilation]  video  time  youtube  art  digital_arts  collage