ts of the Film That Make the Cut" extended="How scenes from five of the nine films were reassembled to promote the films. - Interactive Feature - NYTimes.com" hash="bb7bb4c9acd53ba21a0d772674272a97" href="http://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/02/19/movies/awardsseason/oscar-trailers.html" private="no" shared="yes" tag="visualization time ! narrative movies [project]" time="2013-02-20T13:41:27Z"/><post description="Bloomberg Billionaires" extended="Different visualization views on the world richest people" hash="850e3fd105020a5d7b343788b2ab19b5" href="http://www.bloomberg.com/billionaires/2012-11-04/mca" private="no" shared="yes" tag="visualization ! economy map [project] !! business statistics" time="2013-02-16T12:30:56Z"/><post description="Genetic Cage Scores" extended="Using genetic code to create paths and sounds" hash="2a2006925f24cacbb3657dee99c89d80" href="http://pono.ucsd.edu/~adam/wordpress/projectplanetaria/archives/151" private="no" shared="yes" tag="genetics visualization [post_blog] cybernetics life image code digital_arts algorithm geometry" time="2013-02-15T20:25:56Z"/><post description="Sperm Trajectories, Evolving Humans and a Tomato Tapestry" extended="The Best Scientific Figures of 2012 | Wired Science | Wired.com" hash="e9d13702908221eff2f8bccd4bc412ab" href="http://www.wired.com/wiredscience/2012/12/science-figures-2012/?pid=5582&amp;viewall=true" private="no" shared="yes" tag="visualization [post_blog] [compilation] biology science" time="2013-02-13T23:29:07Z"/><post description="Plaques Map" extended="World Map of commemorative plaques" hash="9fdb4a1ebfcd52998070182b28adce4e" href="http://frankieroberto.github.com/plaques/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="history visualization time text ! narrative map [project]" time="2013-02-13T12:55:27Z"/><post description="Flesch–Kincaid readability test" extended="The Flesch/Flesch–Kincaid readability tests are designed to indicate comprehension difficulty when reading a passage of contemporary academic English. There are two tests, the Flesch Reading Ease, and the Flesch–Kincaid Grade Level. Although they use the same core measures (word length and sentence length), they have different weighting factors. The results of the two tests correlate approximately inversely: a text with a comparatively high score on the Reading Ease test should have a lower score on the Grade Level test. Both systems were devised by Rudolf Flesch. The latter was developed by J. Peter Kincaid for the United States Navy. Such readability tests suggest that many Wikipedia articles may be &amp;quot;too sophisticated&amp;quot; for their readers." hash="33a17df3848b381f9d255f376811921b" href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flesch%E2%80%93Kincaid_readability_test" private="no" shared="yes" tag="information text ! [wikipedia_article] !! code linguistics algorithm" time="2013-02-12T20:45:47Z"/><post description="iWantHue" extended="Colors for data scientists. Generate and refine palettes of optimally distinct colors." hash="5dfbe1bfa150c0d5da7123f4446d4681" href="http://lab.medialab.sciences-po.fr/iwanthue/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="visualization ! color tool [project] code geometry algorithm" time="2013-02-11T22:05:38Z"/><post description="Misleading graph" extended="In statistics, a misleading graph, also known as a distorted graph, is a graph which misrepresents data, constituting a misuse of statistics and with the result that an incorrect conclusion may be derived from it. Graphs may be misleading through being excessively complex or poorly constructed. Even when well-constructed to accurately display the characteristics of their data, graphs can be subject to different interpretation." hash="35e649031d1ffdc86515b2739447499b" href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Misleading_graph" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[wikipedia_article]  visualization  design  information  narrative  " time="2013-02-04T15:44:43Z"/><post description="Arc Diagrams in R: Les Miserables | (R news &amp; tutorials)" extended="Les Miserables characters visualized using arcs" hash="c860a08ac2e622dd7e966547c5d8b0a6" href="http://www.r-bloggers.com/arc-diagrams-in-r-les-miserables/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[post_blog]  [dataRepository]  books  network  graph  visualization" time="2013-02-04T14:27:47Z"/><post description="Flowing City | visualizing the city built of data" extended="compilation of visualization projects about cities" hash="29319f14cb6f2386625cdc26e7b9301b" href="http://flowingcity.com/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="visualization ! [compilation] map !! city" time="2013-02-01T13:04:36Z"/><post description="TimeViz Browser" extended="big compilation of timeline based visualizations" hash="75711ed6f1005d81c832f83deeb4c873" href="http://survey.timeviz.net/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="visualization time ! [compilation]" time="2013-02-01T12:29:20Z"/><post description="Nervous System – explorations in generative design and natural phenomena » Blog Archive » Surface meshing in the browser" extended="A common problem we come across is needing to make meshes of complex surfaces. This can be with many different approaches, but regardless of the method, it is often quite difficult. Especially when doing simulations on surfaces, you need a well-behaved triangle mesh, that is one with an controllable density of elements and nicely shaped triangles." hash="21744e55c6760e2284b38d1b4b1bb6a3" href="http://n-e-r-v-o-u-s.com/blog/?p=3093" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[post_blog]  algorithm  3D  triangle  math  geometry  digital_arts  " time="2013-01-31T10:36:46Z"/><post description="Petri Dish – The Game Of Life Javascript Benchmark" extended="NOW, FOR YOUR AMUSEMENT, a pure Javascript/HTML5 interpretation of computer science classic The Game of Life" hash="ea0f77009f9ae73efe7391e186cc5b72" href="http://www.datapointed.net/2013/01/petri-dish-game-of-life-html5-javascript-benchmark/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="math [post_blog] ! life_game [project] digital_arts simulation algorithm" time="2013-01-30T22:55:42Z"/><post description="Noah Veltman | Infinite Street View" extended="infinite google street maps photos from places" hash="3be447087b34d5ac50cc972af93a3ca8" href="http://noahveltman.com/streetview/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="geography [project] randomness digital_arts photography city" time="2013-01-30T21:33:09Z"/><post description="home.dei.polimi.it/dercole/csr/Dorso_and_Medus_10_IJBC.pdf" extended="The problem of community detection is relevant in many disciplines of science. A community is
usually deﬁned, in a qualitative way, as a subset of nodes of a network which are more connected
among themselves than to the rest of the network. In this article, we introduce a new method
for community detection in complex networks. We deﬁne new merit factors based on the weak
and strong community deﬁnitions formulated by Radicchi et al. [2004] and we show that this
local deﬁnition properly describes the communities observed experimentally in two typical social
networks." hash="98b9c8472009a6def73401f2c1284db9" href="http://home.dei.polimi.it/dercole/csr/Dorso_and_Medus_10_IJBC.pdf" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[pdf]  network  algorithm  math  graph  science" time="2013-01-28T13:41:29Z"/><post description="Hierarchical clustering" extended="In data mining, hierarchical clustering is a method of cluster analysis which seeks to build a hierarchy of clusters. Strategies for hierarchical clustering generally fall into two types:
Agglomerative: This is a &quot;bottom up&quot; approach: each observation starts in its own cluster, and pairs of clusters are merged as one moves up the hierarchy.
Divisive: This is a &quot;top down&quot; approach: all observations start in one cluster, and splits are performed recursively as one moves down the hierarchy." hash="cf49b6ea6ac95e974c438a4140053bfb" href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hierarchical_clustering" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[wikipedia_article]  network  graph  math  algorithm  science  social_network" time="2013-01-28T13:35:39Z"/><post description="Community structure" extended="In the study of complex networks, a network is said to have community structure if the nodes of the network can be easily grouped into (potentially overlapping) sets of nodes such that each set of nodes is densely connected internally. In the particular case of non-overlapping community finding, this implies that the network divides naturally into groups of nodes with dense connections internally and sparser connections between groups. But overlapping communities are also allowed. The more general definition is based on the principle that pairs of nodes are more likely to be connected if they are both members of the same community(ies), and less likely to be connected if they do not share communities." hash="b6d729eba2c737dc0fbdc03b6af42358" href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Community_structure" private="no" shared="yes" tag="math ! graph [wikipedia_article] social_network !! networks algorithm science" time="2013-01-28T13:20:43Z"/><post description="Geometry, Surfaces, Curves, Polyhedra" extended="Great compilation of resources on geometry" hash="ee954399dc590862d5995173f0d9b492" href="http://paulbourke.net/geometry/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="math ! patterns [compilation] 2d !! 3D shape education geometry" time="2013-01-25T15:34:49Z"/><post description="How museums can transform the art of learning" extended="&quot;If we consider that just as the “knowledge economy” defined the 20th century, the “creative economy” will dominate the next.&quot;" hash="c135bef8a31799294823e770e3dcbdb9" href="http://business.blogs.cnn.com/2013/01/24/how-museums-can-transform-the-art-of-learning/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[post_blog] sociology future art museum education science" time="2013-01-25T14:34:00Z"/><post description="Linguistic archeology: The tree of knowledge" extended="expansion of Indo-European languages based on genealogical tree analysis | The Economist" hash="cf150c10e71f8e7820bb29ee8c3982d6" href="http://www.economist.com/blogs/johnson/2012/08/linguistic-archeology" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[post_blog]  language  linguistics  Europe  Turkey  tree  map  statistics  history  time  !  !!  " time="2013-01-23T14:10:12Z"/><post description="" extended="Network tool to navigate Grimm Brothers tales through relations" hash="e9c302f1500976c02f6b5e2769ca5cae" href="http://neoformix.com/Projects/GrimmsExplorer/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="visualization books text graph narrative [project] interface bifurcation networks" time="2013-01-22T17:42:47Z"/><post description="Remix of the Century" extended="XXc songs visualized in a scatter plot / remix able &quot;Remix of the Century is a Music Hackday project by @tomhannen, @indeox, and @hpettersson which aims to explore a century (roughly) of Billboard charts using data from the Whitburn Project.&quot;" hash="e03bd75a0421bcc98668d51f1f7e41e6" href="http://www.remixofthecentury.com/2011/1" private="no" shared="yes" tag="history music visualization time ! 2d [project]" time="2013-01-19T14:40:20Z"/><post description="peoplemovin - A visualization of migration flows" extended="bipartite network of world migrations" hash="50f2a75ab26ad570b8833c822a869298" href="http://peoplemov.in/#!" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[project]  visualization  network  travel  economy" time="2013-01-18T13:14:49Z"/><post description="Plan du métro interactif" extended="isochronic map of Paris métro " hash="0cca21e0e018ef4d8727f11a5bb79c9a" href="http://www.jeromecukier.net/projects/metro/map.html#102" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[project]  visualization 