d="In fractal geometry, the Minkowski–Bouligand dimension, also known as Minkowski dimension or box-counting dimension, is a way of determining the fractal dimension of a set S in a Euclidean space Rn, or more generally in a metric space (X, d)." hash="2458a983fd5104d0ff200b13ea942527" href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minkowski%E2%80%93Bouligand_dimension" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[wikipedia_article]  fractals  geometry  algorithm  2D  topology  complexity  " time="2013-01-09T12:19:17Z"/><post description="Turtle graphics" extended="Turtle graphics is a term in computer graphics for a method of programming vector graphics using a relative cursor (the &quot;turtle&quot;) upon a Cartesian plane. Turtle graphics is a key feature of the Logo programming language." hash="5b8462aae23239ab8d8c35aff74e210a" href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turtle_graphics" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[wikipedia_article]  code  technology  geometry  digital_arts  " time="2013-01-09T12:14:23Z"/><post description="Women as Academic Authors, 1665-2010" extended="Women’s presence in higher education has increased, but as authors of scholarly papers—keys to career success—their publishing patterns differ from those of men. Explore nearly 1,800 fields and subfields, across four centuries, to see which areas have the most female authors and which have the fewest, in this exclusive Chronicle report." hash="180038ed5a3dea2463245b3a918d021b" href="http://chronicle.com/article/Woman-as-Academic-Authors/135192/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[project]  visualization  information  statistics  sociology  science  history  time  " time="2013-01-07T15:07:30Z"/><post description="toys" extended="tutorials to create tens of interactive toys" hash="db9beccc8ed7bdc2f4b37c49c40126a6" href="http://durealeyes.com/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[compilation]  toy  games  education  tutorial  art_craft  3D  " time="2013-01-07T12:30:54Z"/><post description="How to Fold a Julia Fractal — Acko.net" extended="alternative introduction to complex numbers" hash="4f78ed6f6678dcf1e6d8ab209b4ff651" href="http://acko.net/blog/how-to-fold-a-julia-fractal/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[post_blog]  numbers  math  education  geometry  " time="2013-01-07T12:06:56Z"/><post description="The Art of Creative Coding | Off Book | PBS" extended="short documental about creative coding" hash="c635d3e0518f73e6e56cd30b6540f9c3" href="http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eBV14-3LT-g&amp;feature=player_embedded" private="no" shared="yes" tag="processing games 3D interface interaction code digital_arts art [video_youtube]" time="2013-01-07T11:55:43Z"/><post description="Markov chain" extended="A Markov chain, named after Andrey Markov, is a mathematical system that undergoes transitions from one state to another, between a finite or countable number of possible states. It is a random process usually characterized as memoryless: the next state depends only on the current state and not on the sequence of events that preceded it. This specific kind of &quot;memorylessness&quot; is called the Markov property. Markov chains have many applications as statistical models of real-world processes." hash="b8ea1ec32972200634448befbce10999" href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Markov_chain" private="no" shared="yes" tag="math networks information text [wikipedia_article] ! graph randomness !! linguistics statistics science" time="2013-01-06T12:13:31Z"/><post description="32 Imaginative And Beautifully Designed Maps" extended="Maps reinvented artistically." hash="d9eaa825a9b272e61bdec6edb1deff35" href="http://www.buzzfeed.com/angelameiquan/32-imaginative-and-beautifully-designed-maps-70fn" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[compilation]  [post_blog]  map  art  gis  geometry  " time="2013-01-05T17:41:13Z"/><post description="crayon creatures - figurines from children's drawings" extended="We Make
Figurines From Children's Drawings

Send an image, Get an object" hash="d65331d68780bfcfa640929cdc2db50b" href="http://crayoncreatures.com/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[project]  3D  sculpture  art  business  art_craft  illustration  " time="2013-01-05T15:43:41Z"/><post description="a9cbf92793378d3f51f19818cf986358 (3800×2300)" extended="decisions tree to sci-fi books" hash="75e39f1b019cdfcd92eee1abab4285bd" href="https://dl.boxcloud.com/bc/1/f96b2760a2d95d5c5ab46e3941d3f16c/JolueqOGpciD6dgYhecNBoVpYxkvmYe1ZLheZor6BF4DUBIelMQTkFwYIys3nIibNIIEHUp447tBZLaXDzIbNQ,,/a9cbf92793378d3f51f19818cf986358/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[big_image]  science_fiction  tree  network  narrative  text  books  visualization" time="2013-01-05T11:55:50Z"/><post description="Data set" extended="A data set (or dataset) is a collection of data, usually presented in tabular form. Each column represents a particular variable. Each row corresponds to a given member of the data set in question. It lists values for each of the variables, such as height and weight of an object. Each value is known as a datum. The data set may comprise data for one or more members, corresponding to the number of rows." hash="227e765d9162371b0b6640647dd5303d" href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Data_set" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[wikipedia_article]  information  technology  visualization  numbers  " time="2013-01-04T19:09:16Z"/><post description="Data science" extended="Data science incorporates varying elements and builds on techniques and theories from many fields, including math, statistics, data engineering, pattern recognition and learning, advanced computing, visualization, uncertainty modeling, data warehousing, and high performance computing with the goal of extracting meaning from data and creating data products. Data science is a novel term that is often used interchangeably with competitive intelligence or business analytics, although it is becoming more common. Data science seeks to use all available and relevant data to effectively tell a story that can be easily understood by non-practitioners." hash="207ce4db5fae11a89391c29ae9b3dcdb" href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Data_science" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[wikipedia_article]  statistics  information  science  engineering  math  visualization  " time="2013-01-04T18:53:51Z"/><post description="Exploratory data analysis" extended="In statistics, exploratory data analysis (EDA) is an approach to analyzing data sets to summarize their main characteristics in easy-to-understand form, often with visual graphs, without using a statistical model or having formulated a hypothesis. Exploratory data analysis was promoted by John Tukey to encourage statisticians visually to examine their data sets, to formulate hypotheses that could be tested on new data-sets." hash="55a61f94ea75fa168b04dcfaf86a5f89" href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exploratory_data_analysis" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[wikipedia_article]  statistics  information  math  visualization  numbers  science  " time="2013-01-04T18:22:59Z"/><post description="Principal component analysis" extended="Principal component analysis (PCA) is a mathematical procedure that uses an orthogonal transformation to convert a set of observations of possibly correlated variables into a set of values of linearly uncorrelated variables called principal components. The number of principal components is less than or equal to the number of original variables." hash="f735dc675b306fc722c1e1ffba437dc6" href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Principal_component_analysis" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[wikipedia_article]  statistics  math  geometry  numbers  " time="2013-01-04T18:16:07Z"/><post description="Eames House" extended="Welcome to the Eames timeline, chronicling the legacy left by the magnanimous time in American art and design that is the Eames epoch. Simply scroll down the page and watch the history unfold before your eyes. This page is rife with resplendent videos, animations and information. Enjoy!" hash="851c39d75b5d96afac666971dd459a2e" href="http://www.eameshouse250.com/timeline.html" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[project] time history design art sculpture architecture ! !!" time="2013-01-04T18:12:31Z"/><post description="30 Charles + Ray Eames Mathematica IBM wall poster" extended="Timeline of math history for a IBM sciences exhibition, created by Charles and Ray Eames" hash="a56db7c5d9f85d29ce9c462446c8d06e" href="http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tMuW7soKIk0" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[video_youtube]  visualization  time  history  design  math  " time="2013-01-04T18:10:15Z"/><post description="mmcnmt.jpg (1972×1130)" extended="timeline visualization of Art history" hash="49af7c2ac37ce0064687cf64c2d68239" href="http://www.arts.rpi.edu/public_html/century/mmcnmt.jpg" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[big_image]  visualization  art  history  digital_arts  time  " time="2013-01-03T13:19:31Z"/><post description="23 animales que te costará mucho ver aunque los tengas al lado" extended="photos of animals mimicked in the background" hash="050843fc6da6d9057919636bb39f7b90" href="http://www.medioambiente.org/2012/12/23-animales-que-te-costara-mucho-ver.html" private="no" shared="yes" tag="animals [post_blog] biology photography image patterns color [compilation]" time="2012-12-30T21:51:15Z"/><post description="Graffiti Taxonomy Paris by Evan Roth, 2009" extended="classification of typographies used in graffitites, documented with photos" hash="91aa55c9138a1257efd29e1bc9eda900" href="http://graffiti-taxonomy.com/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="statistics geometry ! Paris_France photography typography city popular art text [project]" time="2012-12-30T21:17:38Z"/><post description="Desmos Graphing Calculator" extended="online graphics calcultaor" hash="d524ddcbd00591f22d14dd0f572cf561" href="https://www.desmos.com/calculator" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[project]  math  tool  education  interface  geometry  science  " time="2012-12-30T20:46:49Z"/><post description="Citeology - Projects - Autodesk Research" extended="Citeology looks at the relationship between research publications through their use of citations. The names of each of the 3,502 papers published at the CHI and UIST Human Computer Interaction (HCI) conferences between 1982 and 2010 are listed by year and sorted with the most cited papers in the middle. In total, 11,699 citations were made from one article to another within this collection. These citations are represented by the curved lines in the graphic, linking each paper to those that it referenced." hash="c185be4adb0c7b5c0cf90e57d90c9f48" href="http://www.autodeskresearch.com/projects/citeology" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[project]  text  narrative  network  visualization  linguistics  science  !  !!" time="2012-12-24T00:27:23Z"/><post description="ReCode Project" extended="The ReCode Project is a community-driven effort to preserve computer art by translating it into a modern programming language (Processing). Every translated work will be available to the public and contemporary artists to learn from, share, and build on." hash="caa91abf4cae14d617cb3b5386611fd4" href="http://recodeproject.com/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[project]  [compilation]  digital_arts  art  geometry  interface  interaction  processing  code  algorithm  patterns  history  " time="2012-12-23T21:20:03Z"/><post description="Lists Of Adjectives" extended="This site is dedicated to presenting concise information about adjectives. Everything you need to know about adjectives, search for adjectives, and soon - add adjectives in our continually increasing database. More to come!" hash="f5386b843138266e828b01e87820375b" href="http://listadjectives.com/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[dataRepository]  [compilation]  text  narrative  statistics  linguistics  information  !  !!  " time="2012-12-21T19:59:13Z"/><post description="research-quality data sets" extended="This is a bundle that gathers public data sets that might be interesting to researchers in a variety of fields in one place. Curated by data scientist H Manson." hash="0f5054364e1b714b263fbc9eeaae6fb0" href="https://bitly.com/bundles/hmason/1" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[compilation]  [dataRepository]  !  !!  information  science  biology  visualization  statistics  " time="2012-12-21T17:32:04Z"/><post description="Gameplay: Making and Remaking Karateka (1982-2012)" extended="short documentary on the creation of the new version of Karateka (1982)" hash="0b785f2a6ab4a50e0a6b5d735a5ee4d8" href="http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Vq31IwKZkt0&amp;feature=youtu.be" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[video_youtube]  games  narrative  animation  interaction  interface  video  technology  geek  !" time="2012-12-21T17:22:40Z"/><post description="Snow Fall: The Avalanche at Tunnel Creek" extended="Multimedia news chronic of survival in a snow storm, by The New York Times" hash="468c174b6993dda9f0418f65098b6df3" href="http://projects.nytimes.com/2012/snow-fall-preview/#/?part=tunnel-creek" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[project]  image  video  photography  text  narrative  digital_arts  news  " time="2012-12-20T17:06:25Z"/><post description="Hello Little Fella" extended="faces! pareidolia and semi-pareidolia" hash="5bdb8b897ff5899fe1267e27276a6787" href="http://pinterest.com/shashashasha/hello-little-fella/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[pinterest]  [compilation]  image  photography  perception  illustration  brain  " time="2012-12-19T22:14:07Z"/><post description="Text Adventure: Zork Creators Honored With Pioneer Award" extended="Hommage to Zork, text adventure &quot;But in honor of their achievements and their medium of choice, we’ve decided to present the results of our interviews in a text adventure of our own, below. You’ll have to play to find out more.&quot;" hash="0c080436e0886b3afd3481a9bbe8ebac" href="http://www.wired.com/gamelife/2012/12/zork-infocom-pioneer-award/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[project]  [post_blog]  games  history  technology  geek  [game] " time="2012-12-19T22:00:02Z"/><post description="maps" extended="pinterest board about maps, by Jan Willem" hash="0534447c08f178aac16fc304f23a767e" href="http://pinterest.com/janwillemtulp/maps/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="geography information [compilation] visualization gis map [pinterest]" time="2012-12-19T21:30:17Z"/><post description="How long will we live — and how well?" extended="A new analysis looks not only at the number of years we can expect to live, but also at the number of years we can expect to live in good health. In most of the world, life expectancy is longer than it was 20 years ago, but often a smaller percentage of those years will be healthy ones." hash="8cd6bcee84de81da4d90e9a31ffced3a" href="http://www.washingtonpost.com/wp-srv/special/health/healthy-life-expectancy/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[project]  visualization  statistics  sociology  health  " time="2012-12-19T19:37:07Z"/><post description="Recursive Drawing" extended="Tool to draw recursively" hash="eaf3c1047cb9cc3eebc79e73bdbd1ff5" href="http://recursivedrawing.com/draw.html" private="no" shared="yes" tag="! geometry fractals digital_arts interaction interface tool art [project]" time="2012-12-18T22:20:05Z"/><post description="Braitenberg vehicle" extended="A Braitenberg vehicle is a concept conceived in a thought experiment by the Italian-Austrian cyberneticist Valentino Braitenberg to illustrate in an evolutive way the abilities of simple agents. The vehicles represent the simplest form of behavior based artificial intelligence or embodied cognition, i.e. intelligent behavior that emerges from sensorimotor interaction between the agent and its environment, without any need for an internal memory, representation of the environment, or inference." hash="3bb8594189c7afe7a6f39dc1d3640f8d" href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Braitenberg_vehicle" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[wikipedia_article] artificial_life cybernetics artificial_intelligence algorithm simulation" time="2012-12-18T17:07:40Z"/><post description="List of emoticons" extended="This is a list of notable and commonly used emoticons or textual portrayals of a writer's mood or facial expression in the form of icons. The Western use of emoticons is quite different from Eastern usage, and Internet forums, such as 2channel, typically, show expressions in their own ways. In recent times, graphic representations, both static and animated, have taken the place of traditional emoticons in the form of icons." hash="852173ea1ba46cd361077f296b4d5308" href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_emoticons" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[compilation] internet technology digital_arts typography text [wikipedia_article]" time="2012-12-16T14:51:24Z"/><post description="Interactive evolutionary computation" extended="Interactive evolutionary computation (IEC) or aesthetic selection is a general term for methods of evolutionary computation that use human evaluation. Usually human evaluation is necessary when the form of fitness function is not known (for example, visual appeal or attractiveness; as in Dawkins, 1986) or the result of optimization should fit a particular user preference (for example, taste of coffee or color set of the user interface)." hash="544514786f5a365c6d64b3516f98f975" href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Interactive_evolutionary_computation" private="no" shared="yes" tag="! technology interface interaction artificial_life code algorithm science biology life evolution [wikipedia_article]" time="2012-12-15T23:57:07Z"/><post description="Evolutionary algorithm" extended="In artificial intelligence, an evolutionary algorithm (EA) is a subset of evolutionary computation, a generic population-based metaheuristic optimization algorithm. An EA uses mechanisms inspired by biological evolution, such as reproduction, mutation, recombination, and selection. Candidate solutions to the optimization problem play the role of individuals in a population, and the fitness function determines the environment within which the solutions &quot;live&quot; (see also cost function). Evolution of the population then takes place after the repeated application of the above operators. Artificial evolution (AE) describes a process involving individual evolutionary algorithms; EAs are individual components that participate in an AE." hash="86ca3d5f6554d5394bd6d7c7b4bf613a" href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Evolutionary_algorithm" private="no" shared="yes" tag="chaos complexity math science bioinformatics biology bio genetics evolution ! artificial_intelligence artificial_life technology algorithm code emergence simulation life [wikipedia_article]" time="2012-12-15T23:55:53Z"/><post description="CopyPasteCharacter.com" extended="symbols, unicode and special characters organized in sets" hash="13fee2f1386a0180b001b4a34f67e15f" href="http://copypastecharacter.com/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[project]  text  typography  tool  !  !!  !!!  html  technology  " time="2012-12-15T18:51:09Z"/><post description="Asterank - 3D Asteroid Orbit Space Simulation" extended="3D solar system, planets and significant objects (commets and asteroids)" hash="b8d48ce1010400d02484fe418a1f1948" href="http://www.asterank.com/3d/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[project]  3D  interaction  interface  space  astronomy  visualization  !  " time="2012-12-14T19:16:30Z"/><post description="Every animated GIF on Wikipedia" extended="random animated gif from wikipedia" hash="b54e53e2f4213d11ce04f8a4f22b5b43" href="http://www.wikigifs.org/#Blender3D_CircularWaveAnim.gif" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[project]  animation  digital_arts  wikipedia  image  randomness  humor  " time="2012-12-13T18:18:04Z"/><post description="The Data Behind My Ideal Bookshelf" extended="100 people selecting 100 books. Analysis and visualizations" hash="48d90976832d09838c03803f8cfd7ac2" href="http://fredbenenson.com/blog/2012/12/05/the-data-behind-my-ideal-bookshelf/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[post_blog]  visualization  information  statistics  books  narrative  !  " time="2012-12-12T02:57:23Z"/><post description="Exoplanet Discoveries to Date Are Just a Drop in the Bucket: Scientific American" extended="map of discovered exoplanets" hash="4567ddfdb3c3ddc9cc1c312547ce0c80" href="http://www.scientificamerican.com/article.cfm?id=exoplanets-discoveries-to-date-just-drop-in-bucket" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[post_blog]  visualization  astronomy  map  circle  physics  science  " time="2012-12-11T21:24:00Z"/><post description="A Series of Snowflakes" extended="generated fractal snowflakes" hash="528284ec6a1a6eca61b6438fb137767b" href="http://www.subblue.com/blog/2012/12/6/snowflakes" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[compilation]  image  digital_arts  algorithm  emergence  black_and_white  fractals  chaos  complexity  geometry  !  " time="2012-12-07T17:25:40Z"/><post description="dnb_land_ocean_ice.2012.13500x6750.jpg 13.500×6.750 píxeles" extended="The Earth at night" hash="80ef2d7c0bc30298d049936fc61808dd" href="http://eoimages2.gsfc.nasa.gov/images/imagerecords/79000/79765/dnb_land_ocean_ice.2012.13500x6750.jpg" private="no" shared="yes" tag="gis technology photography light map [big_image]" time="2012-12-07T10:10:22Z"/><post description="tf–idf" extended="Tf–idf, term frequency–inverse document frequency, is a numerical statistic which reflects how important a word is to a document in a collection or corpus. It is often used as a weighting factor in information retrieval and text mining. The tf-idf value increases proportionally to the number of times a word appears in the document, but is offset by the frequency of the word in the corpus, which helps to control for the fact that some words are generally more common than others." hash="4aef4d004c8610682f95bdabd898ee96" href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TFIDF" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[wikipedia_article]  text  algorithm  numbers  math  linguistics  " time="2012-12-06T22:09:48Z"/><post description="String metric" extended="In mathematics and computer science, a string metric (also known as a string similarity metric or string distance function) is a metric that measures similarity or dissimilarity (distance) between two text strings for approximate string matching or comparison and in fuzzy string searching. For example the strings &quot;Sam&quot; and &quot;Samuel&quot; can be considered to be similar. A string metric provides a number indicating an algorithm-specific indication of similarity." hash="2e96908392dbfd3f377a4c29bc995c5d" href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/String_distance" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[wikipedia_article]  text  algorithm  math  linguistics  code  numbers  " time="2012-12-06T22:08:47Z"/><post description="Netherlands from Above - Day in the life of a seagull" extended="A day in the life of a single seagull. Watch him take off from his perch by the ocean, then go inland to raid urban back yards. Then for a dip in the sea before returning home." hash="bf6af35af9c942af903eac6d341e8dcf" href="http://vimeo.com/33587018" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[video]  visualization  [project]  Netherlands  animals  animation  map  patterns  geometry  biology  ecology  city  !  !!  map  gis  " time="2012-12-03T19:23:37Z"/><post description="Johnny Cash Has Been Everywhere (Man)!" extended="Johny Cash song's lyrics list of places georeferenced in a map, in real time" hash="87239c0788d6179e973703079a5e571e" href="http://www.iainmullan.com/johnny-cash/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="gis gi map popular text music humor visualization [project]" time="2012-12-03T10:32:19Z"/><post description="Radiolaria - a biologically-inspired design app by Nervous System" extended="design (then buy) your own ear rings with this tool based in 2D continual transformations" hash="0be4cbbf3086504341258cdd3f4865a0" href="http://n-e-r-v-o-u-s.com/radiolaria/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[project] tool interaction design 3D sculpture geometry ! !! art digital_arts art_craft interface" time="2012-11-30T07:58:21Z"/><post description="Eo9kJ.png (1111×1340)" extended="types and platforms in game industry through time" hash="663c2bfaf47ababc303c4da31a3279e4" href="http://i.imgur.com/Eo9kJ.png" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[image]  visualization  time  games  technology  history  " time="2012-11-24T17:46:30Z"/><post description="futureevents_giorgialupi_large.jpg (4000×2007)" extended="timeline id technologies forecast by sci-fi books" hash="a30b2b1facaff6e28faa7678b2ac2b16" href="http://www.brainpickings.org/wp-content/uploads/2012/11/futureevents_giorgialupi_large.jpg" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[image]  [big_image]  time  science_fiction  visualization  narrative  text  technology  sociology  !  " time="2012-11-24T17:45:38Z"/><post description="The Useless Web" extended="random useless website button" hash="7cd7c302772971f96b17e204610e6cd7" href="http://www.theuselessweb.com/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[project]  [compilation]  internet  humor  interaction  design  digital_arts  games  " time="2012-11-20T00:57:57Z"/><post description="Noam Chomsky" extended="Avram Noam Chomsky (/ˈnoʊm ˈtʃɒmski/; born December 7, 1928) is an American linguist, philosopher, cognitive scientist, logician,historian, political critic, and activist. He is an Institute Professor and Professor (Emeritus) in the Department of Linguistics &amp; Philosophy at MIT, where he has worked for over 50 years. In addition to his work in linguistics, he has written on war, politics, and mass media, and is the author of over 100 books. According to the Arts and Humanities Citation Index in 1992, Chomsky was cited as a source more often than any other living scholar from 1980 to 1992, and was the eighth most cited source overall. He has been described as a prominent cultural figure, and he was voted the &quot;world's top public intellectual&quot; in a 2005 poll." hash="f268e833c70a10f7043244dfc9a08e6d" href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Noam_Chomsky" private="no" shared="yes" tag="politics brain artificial_intelligence sociology linguistics language philosophy [person]" time="2012-11-18T22:57:25Z"/><post description="The Language Instinct" extended="The Language Instinct is a 1994 book by Steven Pinker. Written for a general audience, it argues that humans are born with an innate capacity for language. It deals sympathetically with Noam Chomsky's claim that all human language shows evidence of a universal grammar, but dissents from Chomsky's skepticism that evolutionary theory can explain the human language instinct." hash="151b43d7729ff4a25fb73c6fe188e82e" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Language_Instinct" private="no" shared="yes" tag="education artificial_intelligence philosophy brain sociology linguistics language [wikipedia_article] [book]" time="2012-11-18T22:54:20Z"/><post description="The 10,000 Year Explosion" extended="The 10,000 Year Explosion: How Civilization Accelerated Human Evolution is a 2009 book by anthropologists Gregory Cochran and Henry Harpending. Starting with their own take on the conventional wisdom that the evolutionary process stopped when modern humans appeared, the authors explain the genetic basis of their view that human evolution is accelerating, illustrating it with some unexpected examples." hash="3be08d7ae0cd5b509a30038e702adabd" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_10,000_Year_Explosion" private="no" shared="yes" tag="education biology genetics technology history sociology evolution [wikipedia_article] [book]" time="2012-11-18T22:52:57Z"/><post description="The Camera Versus the Human Eye" extended="This article started after I followed an online discussion about whether a 35mm or a 50mm lens on a full frame camera gives the equivalent field of view to normal human vision. This particular discussion immediately delved into the optical physics of the eye as a camera and lens — an understandable comparison since the eye consists of a front element (the cornea), an aperture ring (the iris and pupil), a lens, and a sensor (the retina)." hash="e03cd7ef292c4053f9e39108d3050a86" href="http://www.petapixel.com/2012/11/17/the-camera-versus-the-human-eye/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[post_blog]  light  geometry  brain  perception  image  photography  " time="2012-11-18T19:38:12Z"/><post description="The Future of User Interfaces" extended="In this article are than a dozen potential future user interfaces that we’ll be seeing over the next few years (and some further into the future)." hash="f7528ee7da1eeb96254e5dd8c20cb285" href="http://sixrevisions.com/user-interface/the-future-of-user-interfaces/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[post_blog]  interface  technology  cybernetics  interaction  history  " time="2012-11-18T15:52:34Z"/><post description="The Carp and The Seagull" extended="‘The Carp and the Seagull’ is an interactive short film about one man’s encounter with the spirit world and his fall from grace. It is a user driven narrative that tells a single story through the prism of two connected spaces. One space is the natural world and the other is the spirit or nether world." hash="d30d5714ad062a4fc88190f458b1248e" href="http://thecarpandtheseagull.thecreatorsproject.com/#about" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[project]  narrative  black_and_white  interface  interaction  games  [game]  poetry  digital_arts  " time="2012-11-16T22:44:52Z"/><post description="Wiley: TED: Statistics: Visualizing Data" extended="list of TED videos about information visualization" hash="bc419274e57de82d430bff2390aed068" href="http://www.wiley.com/WileyCDA/Section/id-814251.html" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[compilation]  education  video  visualization  " time="2012-11-16T20:55:55Z"/><post description="personal Knowledge database" extended="Personal Knowledge Database visualizes and allows the exploration of all my internet references that I've been collecting and producing for more than 10 years. Among them are more than 700 projects (including mine), more than 700 Wikipedia articles, hundreds of images and videos, texts and blog posts.

Only the Wikipedia articles conform the fabric of subjects I've been researching and the theoretical background for my work.

Each reference is placed in the interesection of some of seven sets, each one associated to one of these categories: HUMANISM, TECHNOLOGY, LANGUAGE, SCIENCE, INTERFACE, ART and NETWORKS." hash="3ba8b661b5e057c7f0bccec171148593" href="http://intuitionanalytics.com/other/knowledgeDatabase/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="delicious technology wikipedia text tool !! ! ego information geometry moebio visualization [project]" time="2012-11-16T18:24:25Z"/><post description="Life, the Universe and Everything | a journey to the things that matter through information visualization" extended="32 words (things that matter in life) and 32 great visualization projects, curated by Santiago Ortiz" hash="c791f6d9271130c4e1c2f792c0da21bd" href="http://moebio.com/research/lifeuniverse/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="text digital_arts design information image ego moebio [compilation] visualization [project]" time="2012-11-16T18:22:48Z"/><post description="Queerskins - A Novel" extended="multimedia novel (about the beginnings of AIDS)" hash="e9693f8c4a352751c2202e58a7e85843" href="http://www.queerskins.com/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[project]  music  image  photography  digital_arts  narrative  text  poetry  " time="2012-11-15T02:05:19Z"/><post description="wireframe.cc - minimal wireframing tool" extended="Creating elements of your wireframe couldn't be easier. All you have to do is draw a rectangle on the canvas and select the stencil type that will be inserted there. You can do that by dragging your mouse across canvas and selecting an option from a pop-up menu. If you need to edit anything just double-click it." hash="a648eddaed6cbb2351aae4b265377b7d" href="http://wireframe.cc/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[project]  tool  technology  design  code  interface  !  !!  " time="2012-11-14T20:28:27Z"/><post description="Things Organized Neatly: Archive" extended="collection photos of objects neatly organized" hash="4fcbc72dcbd53b0f4fa3d955ed794c71" href="http://thingsorganizedneatly.tumblr.com/archive" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[compilation]  photography  design  image  patterns  geometry  " time="2012-11-14T19:55:36Z"/><post description="100,000 Stars" extended="navigable 3D model of the milky way" hash="2d8d3cb07cdd0eaec12f05ebea5e8235" href="http://workshop.chromeexperiments.com/stars/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[project]  astronomy  physics  light  space  spiral  !  !!  education  3D  interface  interaction  " time="2012-11-14T19:06:20Z"/><post description="roxik" extended="Roxik is the online showcase of Masayuki Kido, who is a web designer and a interactive director. Hope you will enjoy my works." hash="f7de6a4be723c2f0fd40feee35395db3" href="http://roxik.com/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[portfolio]  digital_arts  interface  interaction  art  design  games  !  " time="2012-11-13T15:04:55Z"/><post description="Department of Experimental Psychology | Research | Available documents, data,... | SUBTLEXus" extended="lists of words (&gt;60 000) with frequencies &quot;Word frequency is an important variable in cognitive processing. High-frequency words are perceived and produced faster and more efficiently than low-frequency words. At the same time, they are easier to recall but more difficult to recognize in episodic memory tasks.&quot;" hash="7cd7d758565760ac1a5aa3bbd761f82f" href="http://expsy.ugent.be/subtlexus/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[dataRepository]  text  statistics  english  information  linguistics  !  !!  " time="2012-11-13T01:37:57Z"/><post description="Astronomical symbols" extended="Astronomical symbols are symbols used to represent various celestial objects, theoretical constructs and observational events in astronomy. The earliest forms of these symbols appear in Greek papyri of late antiquity. The Byzantine codices in which the Greek papyri were preserved continued and extended the inventory of astronomical symbols.[1][2] New symbols were further invented to represent many just-discovered planets and minor planets discovered in the 18th-20th centuries." hash="96baaf957eb77b1d2efe79fe493bda83" href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Astronomical_symbols" private="no" shared="yes" tag="typography history physics text astronomy [wikipedia_article]" time="2012-11-12T22:44:33Z"/><post description="Wiktionary:Frequency lists" extended="Counting words and lemmas: The following frequency lists count distinct orthographic words, including inflected forms. For example, the verb &quot;to be&quot; is represented by the conjugations &quot;is&quot;, &quot;are&quot;, &quot;were&quot;, etc." hash="a73f711d7b2cf5eca01de7e5852dd7f2" href="http://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Wiktionary:Frequency_lists#TV_and_movie_scripts" private="no" shared="yes" tag="! frequencies information tool statistics english text [compilation] [wikipedia_article]" time="2012-11-09T21:26:03Z"/><post description="MTA.ME" extended="Beautiful subway map in which lines are sonified strings" hash="6292274d72e851dbfb04e886b57080a8" href="http://mta.me/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[project]  visualization  map  travel  city  New-York_USA  !  !!  geometry  gis  sound  music  interface  " time="2012-11-09T13:19:57Z"/><post description="Paula Scher Maps" extended="Hand made maps based on text (his father was a cartographer)" hash="d9dbec2a6800cdd5a93be51238947553" href="http://www.paulaschermaps.com/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="color poetry narrative text art map [portfolio]" time="2012-11-08T15:49:07Z"/><post description="The Information: A History, a Theory, a Flood" extended="Gleick begins with the tale of colonial European explorers and their fascination with African talking drums and their observed use to send complex and widely understood messages back and forth between villages far apart, and over even longer distances by relay. Gleick transitions from the information implications of such drum signaling to the impact of the arrival of long distance telegraph and then telephone communication to the commercial and social prospects of the industrial age west. Research to improve these technologies ultimately led to our understanding the essentially digital nature of information, quantized down to the unit of the bit (or qubit)." hash="2d30c44b2d15f96bf54706251d675e30" href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Information:_A_History,_a_Theory,_a_Flood" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[book] [wikipedia_article] information philosophy technology history code education cybernetics math text ! !! brain" time="2012-11-02T14:32:57Z"/><post description="The Nature of Code" extended="Can we capture the unpredictable evolutionary and emergent properties of nature in software? Can understanding the mathematical principles behind our physical world help us to create digital worlds? This book focuses on the programming strategies and techniques behind computer simulations of natural systems using Processing." hash="f802087ff3dced5d637b1c0cfd5b6e76" href="http://natureofcode.com/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[book]  design  art  digital_arts  emergence  fractals  chaos  code  tutorial  processing  math  geometry  education  !  " time="2012-11-02T14:30:44Z"/><post description="Visualize any Text as a Network - Textexture" extended="Welcome to Textexture. Using this tool you can visualize any text as a network. The resulting graph can be used to get a quick visual summary of the text, read the most relevant excerpts (by clicking on the nodes), and find similar texts." hash="064069169f70f741f30fba8913923fac" href="http://textexture.com/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[project]  tool  network  text  graph" time="2012-11-01T13:30:37Z"/><post description="What Age Do Musicians Die at" extended="musicians by different categories, death ages distribution" hash="0c0125f7b00f87952a18073e97eb4ba5" href="http://geeksta.net/visualizations/age-musicians-die/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[project]  music  popular  statistics  visualization  life  " time="2012-10-31T20:51:28Z"/><post description="BBC - A History of the World" extended="A History of the World was a 2010 partnership between the BBC and the British Museum, involving schools, museums and audiences across the UK. This website features all the objects added to the project during the year both by museums and individuals." hash="2a208e1ca803e2eb6e3caa4c51d41a12" href="http://www.bbc.co.uk/ahistoryoftheworld/explorerflash/?timeregion=7#/home" private="no" shared="yes" tag="3D design art_craft art sculpture history interface [project]" time="2012-10-31T02:27:44Z"/><post description="VisWeek Poster: Beatles Genome Project" extended=" Douglas J. Mason, a data visualization professional and Beatles fan, created the Beatles Genome Project Part I and Part II.

Douglas did some complex clustering analysis on the chords, beat, and scale of the Beatles’ songs, inspired by techniques used in bioinformatics. One thing his analysis makes clear is that unusual chords are used by themselves as sort of accents or unique points in songs.  | Visual.ly Blog" hash="c655529a31b415b1becca8c3a6e16f4e" href="http://blog.visual.ly/visweek-poster-beatles-genome-project/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[post_blog]  visualization  music  genetics  statistics  text  " time="2012-10-29T22:12:12Z"/><post description="The History of Film by HistoryShots" extended="This graphic chronicles the history of feature films from the origins in the 1910s until the present day. More than 2000 of the most important feature-length films are mapped into 20 genres spanning 100 years. Films selected to be included have: won important awards such as the best picture Academy Award; achieved critical acclaim according to recognized film critics; are considered to be key genre films by experts; and/or attained box office success." hash="dbef6e8a1727585869bfedc19ba84467" href="http://www.historyshots.com/film/index.cfm" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[project]  visualization  history  time  movies  flow  " time="2012-10-29T15:53:33Z"/><post description="Aviz Research/Passive Physical Visualizations" extended="compilation of data sculptures. &quot;This page is about passive (no electronics included) physical visualizations.&quot;" hash="45dca83cacaf32514862a1c754f88005" href="http://www.aviz.fr/Research/PassivePhysicalVisualizations" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[compilation]  visualization  sculpture  3D  art_craft  art  numbers  information  !  " time="2012-10-29T14:00:57Z"/><post description="Animated Factorization Diagrams" extended="Upon first sight of Brent Yorgey's brilliant Factorization Diagrams, I knew that I should take his lovely little dots and make them dance. – Data Pointed" hash="8b63d0573150bef075e47fd1d01975df" href="http://www.datapointed.net/visualizations/math/factorization/animated-diagrams/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="patterns circle geometry animation numbers math [project]" time="2012-10-29T12:36:54Z"/><post description="Where I Was: An Interactive Map of 9/11 Memory" extended="People round the world respond tha question &quot;where were you on Spet. 11, 2001?&quot;" hash="169745e0eae363b498fb808c863ee85b" href="http://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/09/08/us/sept-11-reckoning/where-were-you-september-11-map.html" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[project]  history  visualization  map  narrative  text  violence  New-York_USA  news  sociology  !  !!  " time="2012-10-27T21:01:52Z"/><post description="Generative art" extended="Generative art refers to art that in whole or in part has been created with the use of an autonomous system. An autonomous system in this context is generally one that is non-human and can independently determine features of an artwork that would otherwise require decisions made directly by the artist. In some cases the human creator may claim that the generative system represents their own artistic idea, and in others that the system takes on the role of the creator." hash="0a0de87b1c9b14a3530beac00afcbea2" href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Generative_art" private="no" shared="yes" tag="design ! algorithm code geometry evolution digital_arts art [wikipedia_article]" time="2012-10-27T17:40:37Z"/><post description="Six Degrees of Black Sabbath #6dobs" extended="Find the path that connects two artists, or find the top connected artists or the strongest connected artists" hash="5f82d151bcc038fd378656ad89a67fbc" href="http://labs.echonest.com/SixDegrees/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[project]  music  popular  network  social_network  !  !!  sound  algorithm" time="2012-10-26T20:40:57Z"/><post description="Jason Davies - Freelance Data Visualisation" extended="portfolio | Math (and other types of) visualization projects" hash="6919167563df8a69ee80e56fab769fa8" href="http://www.jasondavies.com/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[portfolio] math geometry topology visualization numbers interface interaction ! !! !!! map gis sphere" time="2012-10-25T22:05:05Z"/><post description="Random Points on a Sphere" extended="Suppose we want to generate uniformly distributed points on a sphere…" hash="7faf3d58687d7087ecab8e224e7045cc" href="http://www.jasondavies.com/maps/random-points/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[project]  sphere  randomness  geometry  algorithm  code  !  " time="2012-10-25T22:00:25Z"/><post description="Cheshire Cat" extended="…At one point, the cat disappears gradually until nothing is left but its grin, prompting Alice to remark that she has often seen a cat without a grin but never a grin without a cat." hash="eadad7c52cdecba7f945d324c99eaab6" href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cheshire_Cat" private="no" shared="yes" tag="patterns language paradox books narrative animals [wikipedia_article]" time="2012-10-25T18:27:34Z"/><post description="Stop words" extended="In computing, stop words are words which are filtered out prior to, or after, processing of natural language data (text). There is not one definite list of stop words which all tools use, if even used. Some tools specifically avoid removing them to support phrase search." hash="f8671c72ff2b087457b5a92dcc1e105d" href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stop_words" private="no" shared="yes" tag="linguistics language code algorithm text [wikipedia_article]" time="2012-10-25T18:12:37Z"/><post description="This Exquisite Forest" extended="collaborative project where animations are forked" hash="2c38d0898c7996eef17c307751c56d3e" href="http://www.exquisiteforest.com/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="illustration art collective tree digital_arts animation [project] [compilation]" time="2012-10-25T17:44:45Z"/><post description="Unnamed Soundsculpture | Fluid Radio" extended="The basic idea of the project is built upon the consideration of creating a moving sculpture from the recorded motion data of a real person. For our work we asked a dancer to visualize a musical piece (Kreukeltape by Machinenfabriek) as closely as possible by movements of her body. She was recorded by three depth cameras (Kinect), in which the intersection of the images was later put together to a three-dimensional volume (3d point cloud), so we were able to use the collected data throughout the further process." hash="95db9f7fe3ffdd478188d19aef98f88b" href="http://www.fluid-radio.co.uk/2012/03/unnamed-soundsculpture/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[video]  dance  digital_arts  3D  video  music  art  black_and_white  " time="2012-10-25T17:09:29Z"/><post description="The one million tweet map #onemilliontweetmap" extended="A geographical clustering engine for online maps to display and analyse big geolocalized data." hash="0bf7dfc14f99e97d8f45c56ad461afeb" href="http://onemilliontweetmap.com/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[project]  visualization  social_network  text  map  twitter  gis  !  !!  " time="2012-10-25T15:43:20Z"/><post description="Layered MRI Self-Portraits Engraved in Glass Sheets by Angela Palmer" extended="Artist Angela Palmer creates ipeccably detailed three-dimensional views of CT and MRI scans using multiple sheets of vertically layered glass. Just as magnetic fields are used to carefully image layer after layer of internal biological structures inside humans and animals, Palmer etches these same scans into layers of glass. She says her inspiration for these works is a lifelong fascination with maps and visual topographies. | Colossal" hash="966c5884296eb6e5abdf7a07b229ec60" href="http://www.thisiscolossal.com/2012/10/layered-mri-self-portraits-engraved-in-glass-sheets-by-angela-palmer/?utm_source=feedburner&amp;utm_medium=feed&amp;utm_campaign=Feed%3A+colossal+%28Colossal%29" private="no" shared="yes" tag="visualization vis sculpture geometry shape 3D illustration brain art [post_blog]" time="2012-10-25T14:17:49Z"/><post description="Javascript Territory - Jster Javascript Catalog" extended="JSter is a community-driven catalog of the most useful javascript libraries. Find the right tool for a work and do it effectively." hash="1763530cb9c683c3ccd396c956e830c9" href="http://jster.net/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[compilation]  code  tool  technology  !" time="2012-10-24T19:07:50Z"/><post description="Harmonograph" extended="A harmonograph is a mechanical apparatus that employs pendulums to create a geometric image. The drawings created typically are Lissajous curves, or related drawings of greater complexity. The devices, which began to appear in the mid-19th century and peaked in popularity in the 1890s, cannot be conclusively attributed to a single person, although Hugh Blackburn, a professor of mathematics at the University of Glasgow, is commonly believed to be the official inventor." hash="27f75049cc866df511df95e6c57ebbf9" href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harmonograph" private="no" shared="yes" tag="art math geometry art_craft technology sculpture [wikipedia_article]" time="2012-10-24T19:03:45Z"/><post description="84 Million Stars and Counting" extended="Huge photgraphy of the Milky Way. VISTA gigapixel mosaic." hash="bc01709639aa416c4db8bf3af9ad5ead" href="http://www.eso.org/public/news/eso1242/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[project]  zoom  astronomy  photography  space  " time="2012-10-24T13:43:28Z"/><post description="www.viz.tamu.edu/faculty/house/cartograms/Vis98.PDF" extended="A continuous area cartogram is a cartogram 
that is constructed without changing the underlying map topology.  
We present a new algorithm for the construction of continuous 
area cartograms that was developed by viewing their construction 
as a constrained optimization problem.  The algorithm uses a relaxation method that exploits hierarchical resolution, constrained 
dynamics, and a scheme that alternates goals of achieving correct 
region areas and adjusting region shapes." hash="698db7949053bcb55f96f7b62b64d011" href="http://www.viz.tamu.edu/faculty/house/cartograms/Vis98.PDF" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[pdf]  visualization  map  geometry  physics  algorithm  gis  " time="2012-10-24T01:14:08Z"/><post description="How Different Groups Spend Their Day" extended="The American Time Use Survey asks thousands of American residents to recall every minute of a day. Here is how people over age 15 spent their time in 2008. Related article" hash="7c8ea68ad494ae2a5c61aeaf9548ff3f" href="http://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2009/07/31/business/20080801-metrics-graphic.html" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[project]  visualization  time  !  sociology  psychology  !!  interaction  " time="2012-10-24T01:03:58Z"/><post description="Manifest Destiny - The Story of The US Told In 141 Maps" extended="141 maps depicting the territorial changes on the USA history" hash="58b737df35f60628a0aaa18330750e1d" href="http://michaelporath.com/projects/manifest-destiny/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[project]  visualization  map  USA  history  color" time="2012-10-23T20:51:34Z"/><post description="Eloquent JavaScript: A Modern Introduction to Programming" extended="Eloquent JavaScript is a book providing an introduction to the JavaScript programming language and programming in general.

&quot;A concise and balanced mix of principles and pragmatics. I loved the tutorial-style game-like program development. This book rekindled my earliest joys of programming. Plus, JavaScript!&quot;" hash="4825e945aee7522ac6cb84dcdd54b6b9" href="http://eloquentjavascript.net/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[book]  code  tutorial  education  technology  " time="2012-10-23T19:58:24Z"/><post description="Fountain | A markup language for screenwriting." extended="
Fountain is a simple markup syntax for writing, editing and sharing screenplays in plain, human-readable text. Fountain allows you to work on your screenplay anywhere, on any computer or tablet, using any software that edits text files." hash="d8e4f10f22d7861c93a445d132fd1e69" href="http://fountain.io/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[project]  narrative  tool  software  technology  text" time="2012-10-23T18:06:46Z"/><post description="VC blog » Blog Archive » RSA Animate - The Power of Networks" extended="In May 2012, the 12th video of the series was released, based on my talk “The Power of Networks“. The final result exceeded all my expectations, and to this day I’m still dumbfounded by the phenomenal creativity of Andrew Park and his team, and the fantastic visual metaphors they continuously come up with." hash="5309ecbcea402793206dd9211755d4b6" href="http://www.visualcomplexity.com/vc/blog/?p=1125" private="no" shared="yes" tag="visualization  [post_blog]  complexity  networks  animation" time="2012-10-23T17:21:56Z"/><post description="Posted: Visualizing US expansion through post offices" extended="This is a visualization of US expansion in North America from 1700 to 1900, seen through changes in the spatial distribution of post offices.
Data from the USPS Postmaster Finder, with lat/long coordinates extracted from placenames through correlation with the USGS Geographic Names Information System." hash="d424d1034e699c09abe8ae02ef376a0a" href="http://vimeo.com/27376376" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[project]  visualization  map  history  [video]  gis  animation  USA  !  !!  " time="2012-10-23T16:36:28Z"/><post description="Crowdsourcing" extended="Crowdsourcing is a process that involves outsourcing tasks to a distributed group of people. This process can occur both online and offline. The difference between crowdsourcing and ordinary outsourcing is that a task or problem is outsourced to an undefined public rather than a specific body, such as paid employees." hash="26e783427e3f9fb00db6e261f34b8315" href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crowdsourcing" private="no" shared="yes" tag="complexity emergence information community sociology social_network [wikipedia_article]" time="2012-10-23T13:54:35Z"/><post description="27 Ways to Learn to Program Online" extended="Before we delve into our list of learning resources sites, we wanted to share some advice from Marissa Louie, a self-taught product designer for Ness Computing. A former startup founder, Louie told TNW that the hardest part of being self-taught – whether it’s design, programming, or any other discipline is, “gathering the courage. The most important barrier is just to overcome your fears” (she also said having the ability to follow instructions helps as well)." hash="20f515b13fb9a6161b45c7a814b149f4" href="http://thenextweb.com/dd/2012/10/21/so-you-want-to-be-a-programmer-huh-heres-25-ways-to-learn-online/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[post_blog]  [compilation]  code  education  algorithm  tutorial  " time="2012-10-22T17:35:39Z"/><post description="WorldPopulationCube.jpg 1.654×2.339 píxeles" extended="cube template to build a cube with equal-population projection (gridded population cartogram)." hash="9092ef295cea0074bf431f1d4590d751" href="http://www.viewsoftheworld.net/wp-content/uploads/2012/10/WorldPopulationCube.jpg" private="no" shared="yes" tag="population geometry art_craft paper 3D cube ma [image]" time="2012-10-22T10:44:14Z"/><post description="FatFonts" extended="The FatFonts technique is based on a new type of numeric typeface designed for visualization purposes that bridge the gap between numeric and visual representations. FatFonts are based on Indo-arabic numerals but, unlike regular numeric typefaces, the amount of ink (dark pixels) used for each digit is proportional to its quantitative value." hash="944e4d940769f08c2c22377f90fdf75f" href="http://fatfonts.org/?page_id=68" private="no" shared="yes" tag="! geometry design numbers text [project] typography visualization" time="2012-10-20T12:43:25Z"/><post description="Astro Anarchy: An experimental 3D-animation from my image of IC 1396" extended="animated gif of a tridimensional reconstruction of a nebulae" hash="7c9a1a31b544667167a768b1ca2766a2" href="http://astroanarchy.blogspot.fr/2012/10/an-experimental-3d-animation-from-my.html" private="no" shared="yes" tag="animation image astronomy visualization 3D [post_blog]" time="2012-10-19T23:54:32Z"/><post description="The Data-Viz Story Behind Joy Division's Legendary Album Cover" extended="The Data-Viz Story Behind Joy Division’s Legendary Album Cover

IN 1979, DESIGNER PETER SAVILLE CREATED AN ICONIC ALBUM COVER FROM AN UNLIKELY SOURCE: THE FIRST PULSAR READING." hash="d9ce66d650203fcd4205f6e253a3a90c" href="http://www.fastcodesign.com/1671015/the-data-viz-story-behind-joy-divisions-legendary-album-cover#1" private="no" shared="yes" tag="design desi frequencies popular history music visualization [post_blog]" time="2012-10-19T23:01:04Z"/><post description="Marian Dörk" extended="I am a postdoc at Newcastle University in Culture Lab's Digital Interaction group working with Martyn Dade-Robertson on the PATINA project. I am interested in exploring novel uses of interactive visualizations to support a wide range of information practices." hash="05619e68f86364d5a3caec93b42867c5" href="http://mariandoerk.de/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="social_network networks science information visualization [portfolio]" time="2012-10-19T14:17:49Z"/><post description="reMap" extended="eMap displays visualcomplexity.com projects allowing navigation using a semantic approach and depicting relations among them. All images and texts belong to vc portal. Tags are assigned using a semantic engine created by Bestiario." hash="b164714d84ed673642840733afeb51dd" href="http://bestiario.org/research/remap/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="!! ! interaction interface image vc networks ego bestiario visualization [project]" time="2012-10-19T12:25:14Z"/><post description="Experiments in Motion" extended="Experiments in Motion is a research initiative conducted by the Columbia University Graduate School of Architecture, Planning and Preservation in partnership with Audi of America to develop and test new paradigms in the relationship between motion, mobility and design." hash="8f8fb7f83281e847ce82da4c20372111" href="http://blog.experimentsinmotion.com/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="art ar light lig photography city architecture animation [blog]" time="2012-10-19T12:17:45Z"/><post description="catalogtree 4.0" extended="Design and information visualization agency (since 2000)" hash="8049be24670acb0dfeaa66957faebecc" href="http://www.catalogtree.net/" private="no" shared="yes" tag="[institution]  design  visualization  !  Netherlands  digital_arts  art  architecture  photography  " time="2012-10-19T00:16:11Z"/><post description="how old were they?" extended="Directors tend to start their careers later than Musicians.
